Z||000000||JohnF||12-09-2001||12:50 PM||||Who's 85(?)SE was parked at Hurst, Lowe's Hardware Sunday morn.<P>I understand that the SE could be ordered with either a 4 or a 6 but ---- this one has 2m4 on the decklid with dual megaphone exhaust!!!!<P>How did that happen?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||12-09-2001||06:29 PM||||If it had the aero body, it was prolly an 86 or 87 SE. They could be had with a V-6 or a Duke. The 4 cyl SE had a 2m4 decal on the back. Still had the dual megaphones. Just like an Indy.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||12-09-2001||06:46 PM||||I personally have an '85 with the aero body.  Mine says "Fiero GT" on the back (not Fiero 2m4).  Mine has a 6 installed with megaphones on both sides.<P>So, the questions remain, what's up with a SE of any year labeled "2m4" doing with quad megs for exhaust? Decklid change?  Engine change?  Fake exhaust? Other? <P>Who owns this one?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Standard||12-09-2001||07:32 PM||||Both 4 and 6 cylinder aero-bodied SE's got dual exhaust from the factory.  <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
